.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:20:This workflow is exact. Do not silently substitute a different orchestration pattern, runtime, model, monitor cadence, gate, queue behavior, issue bucket, or completion condition. If a blocker prevents completing any required step exactly, stop, escalate, and report the blocker.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:22:Execute each rendered command manually and individually, in the proper workflow sequence, at the moment the workflow requires it. Do not automate the rendered commands with Python, combine them into scripts, batch them together, wrap them in helper programs, or otherwise avoid directly and intentionally running the command yourself.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:26:This section is rendered at goal-creation time using read-only inline commands. Use these concrete values and ready-to-run commands instead of manually rediscovering the Solo instance/project. If `solo_context_status` is `unresolved`, stop and escalate that blocker rather than guessing.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:54:    print("solo_context_status: unresolved")
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:90:    print("solo_context_status: unresolved")
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:104:boomerang = f"/boomerang --rethrow {rethrow} create a goal from template deslop-commit-range for the following commit range {commit_range}"
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:105:print("solo_context_status: resolved")
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:114:print("  preflight_git_status: git status --short --untracked-files=all")
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:133:print("  verify_review_issue_trackable: git status --short --untracked-files=all && git check-ignore -v .ai/issues/review/<created-issue-file>.md || true")
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:142:Before spawning the deslop worker, run the rendered `preflight_git_status` command and inspect the result. If it shows dirty worktree changes, stop and escalate.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:144:Then run the rendered `sentrux_baseline_gate` command, not a bare gate command. It must save the Sentrux baseline and tee the full output into the rendered `/tmp/.../sentrux-baseline.log` path. The rendered command uses `bash -o pipefail` so a failing Sentrux gate still fails the command even though output is piped through `tee`:
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:147:mkdir -p /tmp/<rendered-deslop-artifact-dir> && bash -o pipefail -c 'sentrux gate --save .pi/extensions/goal 2>&1 | tee /tmp/<rendered-deslop-artifact-dir>/sentrux-baseline.log'
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:150:After the gate succeeds, run the rendered `sentrux_baseline_copy_json` command to copy `.pi/extensions/goal/.sentrux/baseline.json` into `/tmp`, not into the repo/cwd.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:163:Use the `spawn_worker` command from the resolved Solo context above. It already contains the concrete Solo instance and project id for this repository. Do not manually rediscover those values unless the rendered context is unresolved or stale.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:173:Use the rendered `send_model_switch` command for delivery, preserving the slash command exactly. It includes a short bounded wait to reduce racey output checks. Before sending the deslop boomerang, run the rendered `verify_model_switch_output` command and inspect the output for evidence that the model switch completed successfully. If the model switch failed or is unclear, retry `send_model_switch` once and then rerun `verify_model_switch_output`. If the second attempt still fails or remains unclear, do not send the boomerang; escalate with the evidence and ask for direction.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:177:Send this exact boomerang command to the worker after the model switch. Prefer the rendered `send_deslop_boomerang` command from the resolved context:
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:180:/boomerang --rethrow {{rethrow}} create a goal from template deslop-commit-range for the following commit range {{args}}
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:183:Do not replace this with a direct prompt, direct `/goal`, direct tool call, or a different template. The spawned agent must receive the boomerang command above.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:189:Use the rendered `arm_timer_pair_60s` command from the resolved context. If you are carrying a TLO run id, add `--run <run_id>` to that concrete command. Confirm the command output shows `check.delay_ms: 60000`; the longer idle sibling timer is expected and does not replace the 60-second check cadence.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:193:When the time-based timer wakes this session, do a token-efficient status check to ensure the worker is still progressing normally.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:195:Use the rendered `timer_pop_on_wake` command and replace `<injected timer body>` with the actual timer body. The rendered command must include the concrete `--project <project_id>` argument; do not rely on `project=<id>` inside the timer body for CLI parsing. Keep routine checks status-first and output-light with `--tail-if never` so a healthy wake does not pull process output:
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:204:Only perform a process-output tail when an issue is suspect, for example stalled state, failed command, unclear completion, repeated identical status, or explicit worker error. If a tail is needed, keep it bounded with the rendered `bounded_tail_if_suspect` command or an equivalent `tlo worker snapshot --tail-if active --tail-lines 40`.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:206:If the worker is active and progressing normally, rearm with the rendered `rearm_timer_pair_60s` command, not a shortened `recommended_next` command that may omit `--check-ms 60000`. Confirm every rearm output shows `check.delay_ms: 60000`, then go idle until the next wake-up. Repeat until the deslop operation is done, the worker has reported, and the worker has gone idle.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:212:After the worker reports completion and goes idle, review the agent report and the actual deslop work/commits yourself. Do not rely on the worker's report as proof.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:218:3. Rerun the Sentrux gate with the rendered `sentrux_post_deslop_gate` command and compare against the step-0 `/tmp` baseline evidence, specifically checking quality score and coupling measurement for degradation:
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:221:   bash -o pipefail -c 'sentrux gate .pi/extensions/goal 2>&1 | tee /tmp/<rendered-deslop-artifact-dir>/sentrux-post-deslop.log'
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:233:### 6. Convert non-deslop follow-ups into review issues and/or queued issue-doc goals
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:240:2. If the nature of the issue is clear and unambiguously needs attention, queue a goal for it with a concrete `create-issue-doc` template invocation that includes bucket, kind, title, and context. Use this objective shape:
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:243:   create a goal from template `create-issue-doc` with args `--bucket review --kind <fix|feature|docs|research|remediation> --title "<short title>" -- <clear issue context, evidence, affected files, and desired outcome>`
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:246:   Do not queue underspecified prose such as only `create a goal from template create-issue-doc for the issue ...`; the queued item must carry enough structured inputs for `create-issue-doc` without guessing.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:248:At this point, you should have either created a `.ai/issues/review/` issue doc directly, queued one or more orchestration-type goals (goals where the goal is to create another goal(s)) which would now be present in the `/goal queue` output list, or both. For every review issue doc created directly, run the rendered `verify_review_issue_trackable` command with `<created-issue-file>` replaced by the actual filename so git visibility is verified.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:254:### 7. Execute queued issue-doc goals when present
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:256:If this process queued one or more `create-issue-doc` orchestration goals, begin executing them now. Work until the queue is finished and all immediate follow-up docs are completed and execution-ready.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:258:Use the existing goal queue semantics safely:
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:260:- do not discard queued work;
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:261:- route `create-issue-doc` orchestration through the reusable template rather than treating it as a direct one-off goal;
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:262:- dequeue orchestration items only after the corresponding issue-doc work is actually satisfied.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:264:When the queue is finished and all follow-up docs are complete/execution-ready, stop and report what was done. At that point this higher-order goal is satisfied as complete.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:271:- step 7 applies: all queued follow-up issue-doc goals from this process have been executed, the queue is finished, and all follow-up docs are execution-ready.
.ai/.pi-goals/deslop-pipeline.md:273:Before marking complete, perform a completion audit that maps every step above to concrete evidence: commands run, preflight dirty-worktree status, timer-pair events, worker process id, final worker report, Sentrux baseline and post-deslop comparison, validation results, commits reviewed, issues fixed, review-bucket docs created, review-doc trackability checks, queue items created/executed, timer pair cleanup/resolution, and remaining blockers if any and output as table(s) in chat. If any timer pair remains active at closeout, use the rendered `cancel_timer_pair_if_active` command with the actual pair id or otherwise prove the pair is already resolved/cancelled.
